-- Translated from ~/.agents/skills/delegate/SKILL.md; instruction wording retained.
fact harness : Harness session
--| Delegate independent lookups, research, reviews, prototypes and chores to Pi in Herdr.
delegate : Skill Unit Unit
delegate =
  - Scripts are in `~/.agents/skills/delegate/scripts/`
  - Write a standalone brief with the task, sources and acceptance criteria
    - Lookup: use `--model light`; ask for `file:line` or URLs
    - Research: use `--rift research/<slug>`; follow `research`; commit and push `docs/research/<slug>.md`
    - Review: name the diff or branch; ask for `file:line`, what breaks and how
    - Prototype: use `--rift prototype/<slug>`; follow `prototype`; push; ask for run instructions
    - Chore: use `--rift chore/<slug>`; commit
  - `spawn <name> <brief.md> [--rift <branch>] [--model light|hard] [--cwd <dir>]`
    - Use `--rift` for all repo writes; it copies the checkout with uncommitted work
    - Use `hard` for verification or when the default fails; tiers are in `models`
  - `await <job> [minutes=60]`; it prints the TL;DR and the next step
    when harness == ClaudeCode
      - In Claude Code
        - Run each `await` with Bash `run_in_background`, one per job
        - Return to the user; the exit wakes you
    else
      - Outside Claude Code: poll until the job ends or the user must decide
    - When done, inspect the actual work
      - Read `result.md` only for detail you need
  - `followup <job> "message"`, then `await` again
  - `land <job>` copies a Rift branch into the source repo; it does not merge
    - Before you merge more than small docs, spawn a `hard` adversarial verifier
      - Tell the user the findings that have evidence
  - `finish <job>` when no work remains, also for read-only jobs
    - It closes the tab and removes the Rift; it keeps branches and reports
    - Do not finish blocked or unresolved jobs
  - After compaction, run `jobs` to see state
    - Start `await` again for each unfinished job
